<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bēbrȳces</span></b> ,
			cum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βέβρῦκες</span> [perh. of kindred origin with the preced.],
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in</i>
			Gallia Narbonensis, <i>on the Pyrenees</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
				423 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bēbryx</span></b> ,
				ȳcis, m., <i>a
				Bebrycian;</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ̓ ἐξοχήν</span>, <i>an
				ancient king of the Bebrycians</i>, <i>whose
				daughter Pyrene gave name to the mountains there</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
			423</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bēbrycĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>pertaining to King Bebryx</i>, <i>Bebrycian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 443</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Pyrene</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					420</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>